"Iteration 1 makes four general fixes to the engine. Broad line-F1 on the 13 scans the engine can run is now **0.832** family-macro (best F1 lane on the same scans: 0.649), and the synthetic regression tier still passes with gates essentially identical to iteration 0. G2 still FAILs overall, mainly because 13 cases are still refused until the G3 truth table is frozen; its known-good flange sub-gate (d) now passes.\n\nThe snapshot was taken before any edit (`engine_before.tgz`). All engine edits are in five files under `domains/production/engine/inspect/`; `eval/` and `compile/` are untouched. The engine version is now e3-1.2.0. Iteration 0 was the baseline and the last generality check was null, so nothing needed reverting or removing.\n\n**What changed, and why:**\n1. **Non-round datum holes (registration).** Five scans were rejected as \"wrong part\": 38172000 X/V, 37361005, 49024000 and 34499000.\n   - **Cause:** slots and windows were treated as circles about their centroid. A rectangle counted as round because its corners are equidistant from the centre, so the \"hole is filled\" test hit solid material.\n   - **Fix:** a hole is round only if its area matches a circle. Other holes anchor the registration through their straight edges, and any part of a hole that compiled stage material occupies (e.g. a tab lying flat in a window at stage 0) is ignored.\n   - **Result:** all five now inspect normally, and the Gold11 cases among them score 31/31 on the relabel with 0 false positives.\n2. **Bend-line position when the datum leaves one direction free (49204020, 15651004).** Every position was withheld. Now a position is measured when it doesn't depend on the free direction; the others stay UNKNOWN(REGISTRATION_UNTRUSTED). 49204020 recovers 8 of 12 lines and 15651004 recovers 1 of 3.\n3. **Flange length on stepped, notched or tapered far edges.** Each station is now compared with the CAD nominal at that position. The false FAIL on 15651004 B3 is gone, sides deviating by more than 0.5 mm drop from 12 to 3 on the affected scans, and G2(d) known-good flange P95 goes from 1.22 mm to 0.52 mm (PASS).\n4. **Flange displaced more than the \u00b13 mm search window.** A wider fallback search now finds it. 50757000 sc_752e decodes 9/9 bends instead of a false half-formed B1 with five unknown bends below it. It reports a real defect: B1 is about 4.9 mm off nominal.\n\n**Results (consumed development scans, frozen scorer, engine vs best F1 lane on the same scans):**\n\n| Population | Iter 0 | Iter 1 | Best F1 lane |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Broad, all 26 cases (13 refused count as misses), family-macro / micro | 0.319 / 0.282 | **0.626 / 0.569** | 0.543 / 0.508 |\n| Broad, 13 runnable scans, family-macro / micro | 0.406 / 0.462 | **0.832 / 0.816** | 0.649 / 0.620 |\n| G2(a) Gold11 relabel, 4 cases run | 0.000 | **1.000** | 0.561 |\n| G2(a) Gold11 relabel, all 9 | 0.000 | **0.574** | 0.547 |\n| G2(a) human Gold11, 4 run / all 9 | 0.000 / 0.000 | 0.724 / 0.467 | 0.717 / 0.473 |\n| Gold set v1, micro / family-macro | 0.491 / 0.440 | **0.961 / 0.936** (0 false positives) | 0.597 / 0.653 |\n\n- **Per-bend correctness given CAD** (report-only proxy, 80 bends): 0.25 \u2192 0.713; every bend is now decoded formed with its angle measured.\n- **False-PASS proxy:** still 17. Eleven are bends whose line matches the relabel but not the broad gold (a gold-convention difference). Six are bends whose position is withheld but whose angle and flanges pass.\n- **Remaining broad misses (16):** gold convention on 11979003, 38172000 and 37361005; the free datum direction on 49204020 and 15651004.\n\n**Gates:**\n- **G1 regression tier (50 cases):** PASS. Only flange bias moved (0.00933 \u2192 0.00938 mm). Six notched-flange measurements shifted by at most 0.004 mm.\n- **G2:** FAIL; G3: NOT_EVALUABLE. The failures and the not-evaluable verdict come from the 13 refused cases plus one case whose CAD compile is blocked. Coverage is 100% on every runnable G2 case. Runtime P95 is 19.6 s and peak engine memory 0.94 GiB.\n- **G5:** not re-run. Nothing under `backend/`, `domains/bend/` or `scripts/` was touched. The known G5 failure comes from another workflow's edit and is unrelated.\n- **Tests:** new `tests/test_prod_engine_inspect_a1.py` (10 passed); existing engine unit, CLI, physical-evaluator and contract-parity tests all pass.\n\n**Decisions and risks:**\n- **Flag semantics changed (fix 2).** `registration.in_plane_degenerate` is now set only when no bend position at all can be determined, because the frozen contract forbids any measured position under that flag. When only one direction is free, the flag stays false, the affected positions and the heatmap are withheld, and a new warning `IN_PLANE_POSE_PARTIAL` is added. UI and PDF readers that treat the flag as \"pose degenerate in any direction\" will see false; R1 should review this.\n- **Displaced-flange search (fix 4) is untested on staged real scans.** It could in principle lock onto a parallel feature next to a bend that is actually unformed. No synthetic case changed.\n- **Weaker check for non-round holes.** A non-round hole now counts as filled only when material covers at least 30% of its open interior, so a wrong part with a partly closed window could pass that check.\n- **No part-specific logic.** Every new rule is geometric and nothing new reaches the engine as input. The gate thresholds are unchanged.\n\n**Biggest remaining lever:** freezing and recording the G3 truth table, so the 13 refused cases can run. `docs/production/ENGINE_INSPECT.md` still lists the old algorithm ids; that document has another owner.\n\nFiles are in `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/a1/iter_1/`:\n- `CHANGE.md`\n- `engine_before.tgz`\n- `engine.diff`\n- `raw/`\n- `overlays/`\n- `diag/`\n- `tools/`\n\nNew test: `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/tests/test_prod_engine_inspect_a1.py`\n\nThe work directory is `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-idantal/db065cf7-f766-4885-b217-ed8d7edd7ade/scratchpad/a1_iter1`."